  "name": "Alcohol Use Disorders Identification Test (AUDIT)",
  "short_name": null,
  "language": "en",
  "description": "The Alcohol Use Disorders Identification Test (AUDIT) is a 12-item self-report screening questionnaire designed to measure harmful alcohol use (Saunders et al., 1993a). This includes the 10 standard questions of the AUDIT and 2 questions at the end to determine self-identified problem drinking and self-perceived difficulty in stopping drinking.",
